@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# Deterministic NixOS module workspace
+
+Nix Software Center compiles the NixOS `options.json` documentation database into UI-ready module metadata. The pipeline is deterministic and does not use an LLM, Wingless, or another generative service.
+
+## Pipeline
+
+```text
+nix-data::cache::nixos::nixosoptions()
+                    |
+                    v
+             options.json
+                    |
+                    v
+        parse::modules::load_catalog
+                    |
+                    v
+              ModuleCatalog
+                    |
+                    v
+          GTK Modules workspace
+          /       |          \
+     search    generated     advanced/
+               controls      read-only
+                    |
+                    v
+        staged ManagedModuleState
+                    |
+                    v
+          generated Nix preview
+                    |
+                    v
+ /etc/nixos/nix-software-center-modules.nix
+                    |
+                    v
+       nsc-helper managed-config
+                    |
+          nixos-rebuild test
+                    |
+                    v
+          nixos-rebuild switch
+```
+
+## Module discovery
+
+A module root is discovered only when a non-dynamic boolean option ends in `.enable`. Options are assigned to the most specific enclosing root. Dynamic `<name>` paths, submodules, functions, unknown types, and collection types that require embedded package/path expressions fail closed to the `advanced` renderer.
+
+The compiler preserves the original Nix type string, default/example metadata, description, declaration paths, read-only state, nullability, and dynamic-path state.
+
+## Generated editors
+
+The GTK workspace renders supported option metadata into controls for:
+
+- booleans;
+- documented choices;
+- integers and finite floating point values;
+- strings;
+- paths;
+- nixpkgs package attribute paths;
+- JSON-backed primitive lists;
+- JSON-backed primitive attribute sets.
+
+Unsupported or ambiguous option types remain visible but are marked **Advanced** instead of being guessed into a writable control.
+
+Every generated option supports reset-to-default semantics. Changes are staged across module selections and the complete generated Nix file can be inspected before Apply.
+
+## Managed configuration boundary
+
+The module workspace never rewrites arbitrary `configuration.nix`. The NixOS installation integration imports one NSC-owned file:
+
+```text
+/etc/nixos/nix-software-center-modules.nix
+```
+
+The file contains both the generated Nix assignments and a one-line JSON state marker. The application reads only that marker on restart; it never attempts to reverse-parse arbitrary Nix syntax.
+
+The installer is responsible for importing the managed file once. If that integration file is not present, module browsing remains available but Apply is disabled.
+
+## Transactional rebuild
+
+`nsc-helper managed-config` owns the privileged transaction:
+
+1. preserve the previous managed file;
+2. write the candidate generated file from stdin;
+3. run `nixos-rebuild test`;
+4. only if test succeeds, run `nixos-rebuild switch`;
+5. if either step fails, restore the previous file;
+6. best-effort switch back to the restored configuration;
+7. only prune generations after a successful switch.
+
+The existing package installer is unchanged.
+
+## Benchmark / inspection utility
+
+On a NixOS development host:
+
+```bash
+cargo run --bin nsc-module-index -- --system /tmp/nsc-modules.json
+```
+
+Or against a specific option database:
+
+```bash
+cargo run --bin nsc-module-index -- /path/to/options.json /tmp/nsc-modules.json
+```
+
+The utility prints module/option coverage and elapsed compiler time. Supplying an output path writes the deterministic catalog as JSON for inspection.
+
+## Focused acceptance
+
+```bash
+cargo fmt --check
+cargo test parse::modules::tests
+cargo test parse::modules::managed_tests
+cargo test -p nsc-helper
+cargo run --bin nsc-module-index -- --system /tmp/nsc-modules-a.json
+cargo run --bin nsc-module-index -- --system /tmp/nsc-modules-b.json
+cmp /tmp/nsc-modules-a.json /tmp/nsc-modules-b.json
+cargo build
+```
+
+Then launch the application on NixOS, open **Modules**, stage a reversible option change, inspect the preview, Apply, and verify the rebuild dialog reports `test` followed by `switch`.
+
+## Deliberate boundaries
+
+The current editor does not attempt to synthesize values for dynamic submodules or arbitrary raw Nix expressions. Those remain advanced/manual territory until they receive purpose-built deterministic editors.
